      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_d0084130506b39a719bc5d50cc27b4c5012d387132dddec344ba5580725ae806",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The reported computation has three distinct dependencies: bounded strong-pseudoprime implications for treating tested candidates as prime, the logical equivalence between shifted primality bits and covered Goldbach targets, and the correctness of the implementation and run that performed all required shifts. Word-level OR operations accelerate the second mechanism but do not themselves establish that the complete run was executed correctly. Thus the span supplies reported exhaustive computational evidence for its finite range, not an independently inspectable certificate: its narrative includes no code, logs, replay result, or retained final coverage array.",
