    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f04d9e231a12118fed7c4ca5c66bb355dc3cda092d2efd8b358e987786e16a1b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The GRH-dependent asymptotic argument covers odd inputs above its stated threshold; below that threshold, the short-interval lemma supplies a prime p for which the even remainder m=n-p is at most about 1.615 x 10^12, and the reported binary Goldbach verification through 10^13 supplies m=p1+p2. The strict overlap of those bounds composes the analytic and finite regimes into n=p+p1+p2.",
